From: Zaman OS maintainers <opensource@kawnelectro.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep process alive while handling SIGINT

ConsoleCancelEventArgs.Cancel defaults to false. Returning from the
CancelKeyPress handler without changing it therefore terminates the process
before the close operation posted to Avalonia's UI thread is guaranteed to
run.

Cancel the runtime's default termination and let CloseEmu(true) perform the
normal shutdown path. This allows MesenCE to flush battery-backed saves,
write the recent-game recovery archive, save configuration, and close its
window before exiting normally.

Upstream-Tag: 2.2.1
Upstream-Commit: 20ba206cef5ba207c21203176d02cb9f43dda9fb
diff --git a/UI/Windows/MainWindow.axaml.cs b/UI/Windows/MainWindow.axaml.cs
index 4f0728e..2cda856 100644
--- a/UI/Windows/MainWindow.axaml.cs
+++ b/UI/Windows/MainWindow.axaml.cs
@@ -190,0 +191 @@
+			e.Cancel = true;
